## CH 9 — Hikawa Shrine, Rei POV, day 1 of renovation

- **Trigger:** Estate finalized. After tax/lawyers/townhouse sale: **¥61,400,000**. Untouched 11 months. Ward assessor letters (3 yrs, "advisory/notice") under a **gray river stone** paperweight on the shamusho desk. Ceiling stain grown to blistering plaster.
- Rei calls Byl off his handwritten invoice (blocky pencil, **crossed sevens**, labor to the quarter hour). He's in an Itabashi basement; arrives 12:52.
- **The list (brush, on back of a probate form), 14 items:** 3rd haiden stair step, remaining roof (SW run + main hall), copper gutters + rain chains, chōzuya supply line & pump, torii repaint, storehouse door (dropped hinge, white arc scraped in stone), knob-and-tube wiring in shamusho, water heater, last 40m fence, tilted stone lantern (March quake), suzu bell bracket, ema rack, gravel drainage to kagura-den.
- Byl: "**This is six weeks. If nothing's rotten underneath.**" Asks why him and not a Nakagawa crew. Rei: "You returned my money. Men don't return money." Accepts: same rate, materials at cost, receipts on a clipboard in the storehouse.
- **Rei senses his relief** (fire-sense: a cable going slack, wrapped in shame) — reads unpaid rent, behind more than one month. Looks away so he won't know she knows. Offers to **recommend him to her friends** (one opening a flower shop, knows nothing about ventilation → Makoto seed). He drops the sarcasm: "I'd appreciate that. Really."
- **Respects before work:** full correct chōzuya ritual incl. tipping the ladle to rinse the handle (nobody under 60 does this). **Five-yen coin** (go-en, "connection"). Two bows, two claps. Head bowed **40+ seconds**, shoulders still. Coals shifted in the sealed goma room; Rei felt it on her neck.
- **Lucy admitted.** Sat at the torii line 12 min. Rei: "noble… left outside the gate like a delivery nobody signed for." Byl calls her in; **Lucy looks at Rei, not Byl, before crossing.** Phobos & Deimos call once together, then go silent and track the dog.
- **Step 3 opened:** keyaki tread, stringer riddled with **termite galleries**. Byl puts his ear to the wood and knocks along it to find the extent. Adds **#15 — stringer + inspect sill.** Shores it with a steel jack post; stair closed.
- **Lucy's day:** consoles a crying salaryman (he bows to the dog leaving); belly-up for two office women. Old woman at the omamori window: "A handsome man on the roof, too."
- **3:15 — black tinted Alphard idles at the foot of the steps.** Byl comes down the ladder, stands at the top of the stone stairs with the flat bar in hand, says nothing. Van leaves after 40 seconds. Rei creases an ofuda. **Neither of them mentions it.**
- **MEMORY 1 (4:10, unbidden, light goes silver):** Lucy in a bar of light → same gait, same dog, beside a black-haired boy in pale plate with a sword, still growing. Rei drops the omamori tray.
- **Fire vision — the camping trip.** Five girls, ~11, white silk pavilions at the edge of the dust sea, Earth overhead. Serenity gushing re: Endymion ("forty-two" times per Venus). Guardsman walks the perimeter with the dog. Venus: put Captain **Rhaen** down in four seconds. Jupiter: he called her honey cakes "**fine**" ("*fine* is what you say about weather"). Mercury: youngest ever raised to the Queen's own guard, by two years. Rei: "He calls *me* Your Highness like it's a joke." All wish to marry him; Serenity: princesses can't marry commoners, it's the law. **Rei: "Then we'll make him a prince." "Of what?" "Of us."** He calls: "Go to sleep, Your Highnesses." They shout his name — **the fire eats it; she can't hold it.**
- **Close:** Byl leaves; Rei watches him descend, gets physically aroused (nipples, thighs pressing, wet) and catches herself — 19 years of finding men tiresome; once told Minako she'd rather marry the fire. Adds **#16. The fire. Again, tonight.**

## CH 10 — Shrine, day 2, Rei POV

- Night 1: fire gave **nothing**. Three hours' sleep.
- Lucy now admitted by **a single nod** from Rei at the window.
- **Gutter work:** hand-formed copper half-round, forged fern brackets, deep verdigris. Lowered section by section on a sling, laid on a tarp **in order**, grease-penciled **H1/H2/H3**. Wire-brushed to salmon-pink, flux, propane torch, lead-free solder. H1 finished (clean silver seam), H2 half done. **#17 — soft fascia behind H3** (thumb sinks in). Rei jokes they'll run out of paper; he says use the probate file; **she laughs out loud.**
- **Lucy's age problem, planted:** Byl says ten years this winter, **grown when she found him** — behind a Kōtō warehouse, snowing, he was "sitting on a pallet being stupid," she came around the corner "like she had an appointment" and sat on his foot. **No gray on the muzzle at all.** "Vet says good genes. Vet's been saying it for ten."
- Byl to a loudly praying baseball player: "**Bunt more.**" Boy flees.
- **Lucy escorts Rei to the goma room and lies across the threshold, facing out, back to the fire — posted like a guard.**
- **Fire vision — age 15.** The rivalry is now open flirtation: Venus scratches a **tally in the 4th colonnade column with a hairpin** (looks at the colonnade / looks at *her*). Jupiter sends a basket every third day; returns with notes — *Good.* / *Very good.* / "**I'd die for this**" (kept in her sleeve a month). Mercury beats him at three-layer moonstone lattice every time and is infuriated that "**he makes the same mistake four times and then never again.**" **Rei asked him to teach her the sword; he refused ("You've got fire. What do you need a stick for?" / "Fire can't hold a door"), then taught her only how to stand — feet, knees, weight low, breath — 15 min, three times, at dawn. She never told the others.** He's ~19, legend growing, laughing less, walks the walls at night.
- **Throne room, seen from the disused musicians' gallery** (behind the tapestry of the first Queen receiving the Crystal; screenwork of moonflowers). Rei lies flat.
  - Queen **stands, never sits.** Praises him: Rhaen has nothing left to teach him; Jovian ambassador asked to borrow him twice, refused twice; finest blade in a century.
  - Then: "**My daughters are fond of you… Young hearts are easily turned… I would not have them spend their hearts on a door that cannot open for them.**"
  - He understands instantly. Sets his shoulders. "**Then send me somewhere they can't see me, Majesty.**" Queen: "I had hoped you would say that." ← Rei at 15 read grace; Rei at 19 recognizes **her father's donor-list face** — fond, calm, *measuring*.
  - **Lucille blessed first,** Queen kneeling on the white floor: light poured over her head, eyes turn **silver**, coat glows at the root. "**Wisdom, to find the way when he cannot see it. Strength, the strength of a hundred of your kind… Loyalty you already have. I would not insult you by giving it.**" Lucille licks her wrist; the Queen laughs, surprised.
  - **He kneels.** Both palms on his head, light floods and pools in a silver ring. "**Light as your weapon. Duty as your shield… You will go past the gates, beyond the last world… You are the first line. You may be the only one.**" His eyes change — blue gone hard, ice over deep water.
  - His oath: "**Nothing reaches them. If anything gets through, it walked over what's left of me to do it. I'll die out there before I let anything past.**"
  - Queen says his name → **fire flares, burns the name, ash. Twice heard, twice lost.**
  - Leaving, he stops **under the gallery**, doesn't look up; **Lucille looks straight up at Rei through the screen and wags.** "**Goodnight, Your Highness.**" Not a joke anymore.
- **THE REDACTION — Rei's deliberate search.** Venus's tally column: **smooth stone.** The barracks doorframe: just a door. Jupiter cooking for **no one**. Mercury's game with **no opponent**. The corner of the sand where she learned to stand: **empty** — she has always credited her grandfather for that stance. Holes are **clean-edged, precise, one-man-and-one-dog shaped**, "like a gallery where one painting was taken off every wall and the rectangles painted over to match."
- **Conclusion (cold certainty):** Queen Serenity erased him from all five Senshi. Two guessed motives, both credited: (1) mercy — spare them watching for a patrol that never returns; (2) control — they'd have followed him past the gates (Venus first, Jupiter packing food, Mercury plotting the route, Rei with fire in both hands). She closed the door, took the key, took the memory of the door.
- **Rei concludes he died out there** — Metallia came *through*, so it walked over him; no Crystal that far out to catch his soul; sent as far from it as a man could go. "**Nobody had even remembered to grieve him.**" She breaks down hard (harder than for her father) — grieves the boy **and** the stolen first feeling she never got to lose properly. **Lucy comes in and presses her full body against Rei's back, chin on her calf.**
- **Close:** Byl clocks her red eyes, looks once at the soaked translucent kosode, returns to her face and stays there. "Long prayer." / "Long list." Doesn't ask. Almost says something at the gate, decides against it: "**Get some sleep, Hino.**" Rei sees light off his hand in the dusk for half a second. She lights incense for her father (equinox), then writes a **new plain hinoki spirit tablet: "The Guard of the Gates" / smaller: "and his dog,"** and sets it on the household altar beside her father, mother, grandmother. Crows watch the stone steps long after he's gone.

